{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>The aftergrowth of your harvest.</b> Even if you did not sow it and it grew from seed that fell in it at harvest time — that is called סָפִיחַ." "<b>You shall not reap.</b> So as to hold it like other harvest, but it shall be ownerless to all." "<b>Your undisclosed grapes.</b> Which you held back and kept people away from them and did not declare them ownerless." "<b>You shall not harvest.</b> Them you may not harvest — but from what is declared ownerless you may."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:11.441114658Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}